tion a>b>0 this is choice B, sqrt(a):sqrt(a-b). The geometry only forces the fraction a/b>1; choosing both numerator and denominator negative is a nonstandard representation that would invalidate separate real square roots. Keep that explicit representation qualification and ordinary grading rather than treating it as a newly confirmed defect. Concentricity is unnecessary for area subtraction.","recordedAnswer":"B","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":["The statement does not explicitly require a and b to be positive; choice B assumes a>b>0.","The geometry forces a/b>1 but does not force a and b individually to be positive. Choice B as a ratio of real square roots assumes the conventional representation a>b>0."],"questionId":"1969_AMC_12_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p185","cnm_074","cnm_170","cnm_040"],"id":"subtract-circle-areas","label":"Subtract the circle areas","methodDirectNodeIds":{"subtract-circle-areas":["cnm_p192","cnm_p150","cnm_220"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p192","cnm_p150","cnm_220","cnm_p185","cnm_074","cnm_170","cnm_040"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 14; a/b=7+4sqrt(3).","reason":"For r=a/b>1, r+1=4sqrt(r), giving r^2-14r+1=0. The admissible root is 7+4sqrt(3), approximately 13.928, which rounds to 14.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1968_AMC_12_Q28","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p185","cnm_p121","cnm_170","cnm_148","cnm_079"],"id":"square-root-ratio","label":"Use the square-root ratio","methodDirectNodeIds":{"square-root-ratio":["cnm_211","cnm_h209","cnm_221"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_211","cnm_h209","cnm_221","cnm_p185","cnm_p121","cnm_170","cnm_148","cnm_079"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":7,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D: 10∜8","reason":"Let r = AB/H. The upright area-36 and area-4 rectangles have widths 6/√r and 2/√r. Together they span the area-32 rectangle, whose width is √(32r). Thus 8/√r = √(32r), giving r = √2. The areas sum to 200, so AB = √(200√2) = 10∜8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2024_AMC_10A_Q16","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_268","cnm_169","cnm_170"],"id":"2024_AMC_10A_Q16_m1","label":"Find the common side ratio","methodDirectNodeIds":{"2024_AMC_10A_Q16_m1":["cnm_270","cnm_p089","cnm_p150","cnm_220","cnm_h039"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_270","cnm_p089","cnm_p150","cnm_220","cnm_h039","cnm_268","cnm_169","cnm_170"]}]}],"layer":"ailleo","meaning":"Reviewed content-bound concept practice; no claim of complete source-standard coverage or learner mastery.","nextOffset":null,"nodeId":"cnm_170","status":"mapped","total":12}
